    rw:[["Scout realizes the quiet man in Jem's room is Boo Radley.",0,"Right — this is the story's final surprise."],["Atticus believes Jem acted to protect Scout.",0,"Right — that is why he wants to confess."],["Heck Tate agrees completely with Atticus's plan to confess.",1,"Wrong — he insists on a different story instead."],["Boo Radley has lived a loud, public life in Maycomb for years.",2,"Doesn't say — the opposite seems true, since he is shy and private."],["Heck Tate compares exposing Boo to killing a mockingbird.",0,"Right — he uses this exact comparison."],["Scout feels proud to walk beside Boo Radley.",0,"Right — she feels this while walking him home."],["Scout never thinks about her father's advice again.",1,"Wrong — she finally understands it on the porch."]],
